<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Culture &amp; Lifestyle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-cul</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:52:31Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-cul" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1441?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-cul" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>China's influence in the gaming industry is growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36d5c11d1743691067c71f7630be7aa5a0d55643c90466044765b299ae377d7b</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:52:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T11:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755--447380e7608a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Home to more than 700 million gamers, China is the world's largest gaming market — but it's also one of the most tightly regulated. The effects reach far beyond China, impacting players around the world.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Left-leaning Berlin coalition talks break down</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7a54860fb7c0e39a61463032e50207cbc8f324a54aa70749264a8136746f0d0</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T19:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-left-leaning-berlin-coalition-talks-break-down/live-79647092--70d338313c8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-left-leaning-berlin-coalition-talks-break-down/live-79647092?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The SPD and Greens in Berlin have halted exploratory coalition talks with the Left Party amid a dispute over Israel policy and antisemitism. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Breaking Bad' actor and disability advocate RJ Mitte dies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:103317193a3cbcbcba7f5300f1dfee181193a48e99498cb48c0cf18bbbcbfc5a</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T01:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/breaking-bad-actor-and-disability-advocate-rj-mitte-dies/a-79646725--2e0d60b653fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/breaking-bad-actor-and-disability-advocate-rj-mitte-dies/a-79646725?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">RJ Mitte said his lived experience with cerebral palsy was an asset for his role as Walter White's son Flynn on "Breaking Bad."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK students call for school uniforms to be banned in pornography</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56a476a6ea5ad2cfa8e496eb6b8050a61638ae39e9d71ac890ab6191ec8af9df</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T07:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-students-call-for-school-uniforms-to-be-banned-in-pornography/a-79554324--e21f080b6070.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-students-call-for-school-uniforms-to-be-banned-in-pornography/a-79554324?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Short skirts, knee-high socks, white blouses: Girls' school uniform items are widely used as costumes in pornographic videos. As students experience harassment, a group wants to change that.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>'Ragebait' is the 2026 German Youth Word of the Year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b10eab4e9ff7aeff99e9773ba4d8107025560d7096428d4c0fdfd82d4ff34f44</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158--c39c4c350c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Is China seeking to restrict Taiwan's cultural presence?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f50c3d29b37cb9145c366988e71b7d0ef87127c6a2f87db0cc296ba6bf7d04b3</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T06:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-china-seeking-to-restrict-taiwan-s-cultural-presence/a-79610947--71784c91bb83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-china-seeking-to-restrict-taiwan-s-cultural-presence/a-79610947?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From coffee competitions to literature awards, Beijing appears to be working to limit Taiwan's international cultural and political impact.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Art for freedom: Maria Kalesnikava in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2043d32a6df72948d77fe32dfdaf71275b7b4234b5093387d97aab296fc849f5</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009--0f2314a86e67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Belarusian musician and civil rights activist Maria Kalesnikava held the keynote speech on the importance of art at the 2026 Beethovenfest in Bonn. She also visited DW.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>125 years of Thomas Mann's 'Buddenbrooks'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:228a88072373da80702232c535f3adf99f25af8fceb4111b30819e1da5ca3776</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236--20da98f1ab2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This over 1,000-page masterpiece offers a panoramic view of society in the 19th century and exposes the collapse of a merchant family: unrecognized sons, disillusioned daughters and the loss of middle-class ideals.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Why music in Iran is more than just entertainment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a7212532eb1eca78aee2fd8c7eeafeca2ef1c51dec710fa975959e54118e68e</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T05:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-music-in-iran-is-more-than-just-entertainment/a-79583224--67cbee1305a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-music-in-iran-is-more-than-just-entertainment/a-79583224?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian authorities are trying to persuade prominent singers in exile to return home. While the state seeks to harness music as a political tool, music has also become a powerful expression of dissent and resistance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in literature: How the winner is secretly chosen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e535f6ba926f8cc6f897f395c8c0cd2f63527b7455ee53447544fc3dce8ea8d</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151--0152f72654ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Can Xue is considered one of this year's favorites; Margaret Atwood and Salman Rushdie are other strong contenders. But what goes on behind the scenes in the selection of the Nobel Prize in literature?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>South Park satirist pushes for accountability in Cornell gang-rape lawsuit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f03fb09cce6ece0f0f30073e622fbc71d7859456d828058c4a4dc33b688aaf27</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-park-satirist-pushes-for-accountability-in-cornell-gang-rape-lawsuit/a-79475382--e2bb4e991ce2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-park-satirist-pushes-for-accountability-in-cornell-gang-rape-lawsuit/a-79475382?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Writer Toby Morton is using a new website to amplify allegations in a high-profile sexual assault lawsuit involving seven Cornell students. The reopening of the case is causing an outcry on social media.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecd7c42aad8118ebfe2ec59b00718dfcad642af608cdcd86a54fa342fbae7fa4</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>'90s art scene in the UK: An international, edgy trendsetter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e23244eb90718a7e15fa3a230f62a5c1e6a74f2dbd475a6b47e9c4ce2c293be3</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/90s-art-scene-in-the-uk-an-international-edgy-trendsetter/a-79581777--d9e1246b3502.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/90s-art-scene-in-the-uk-an-international-edgy-trendsetter/a-79581777?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 1990s are remembered for Brit-pop and provocative fashion, but beyond the nostalgia, it was a decade of cultural experimentation and social change. Tate Britain's new exhibition looks past the familiar icons.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
